<title>CANADA: Canadian foreign reserves rise in March.</title>
<headline>Canadian foreign reserves rise in March.</headline>
<dateline>OTTAWA 1997-04-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Canadian foreign reserve holdings rose in March, the Finance Department said on Thursday.</p>
<p>   RESERVES			  Feb 97	Feb 97</p>
<p>   Total			   21.638 bln  21.044 bln</p>
<p>   U.S. dollars		  18.726 bln  18.110 bln</p>
<p>   Other foreign currencies     499 million     505 million</p>
<p>   Gold				 150 million     150 million</p>
<p>   Special drawing rights     1.134 bln   1.132 bln</p>
<p>   IMF reserves		   1.129 bln   1.147 bln</p>
<p>Note - Figures in U.S. dollars.  </p>
<p>Official government operations decreased reserves by US$278 million.</p>
<p>Details of the changes in the month:</p>
<p>    Gain on gold sales		   n/a</p>
<p>    Earnings on investments	    +89</p>
<p>    Revaluation effects		   -3</p>
<p>    Foreign currency debt	     +791</p>
<p>    Other transactions		    -5</p>
<p>NOTE - in millions of U.S. dollars  </p>
<p>During March, net sales of Canada bills totalled $899.4 million, increasing the level of outstanding bills to $6.093 billion. Sales of Canada notes decreased by $108 million, increasing the level of outstanding notes to $1.532 billion.</p>
<p>((Reuters Ottawa Bureau (613) 235-6745))</p>
